Phos-Flur Rinse contains sodium fluoride at a concentration of 0.044% (w/v). How many milligrams of sodium fluoride are present in a 10 mL dose?,"<bos><start_of_turn>user
Phos-Flur Rinse contains sodium fluoride at a concentration of 0.044% (w/v). How many milligrams of sodium fluoride are present in a 10 mL dose?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","To find the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Phos-Flur Rinse, we can use the formula:

\[
\text{Mass} = \text{Concentration} \times \text{Volume}
\]

Given:
- Concentration = 0.044% (w/v) = 0.044 g/100 mL
- Volume = 10 mL

Substitute the values into the formula:

\[
\text{Mass} = \left(\frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}}\right) \times 10 \text{ mL}
\]

\[
\text{Mass} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
\]

Convert grams to milligrams:

\[
\text{Mass} = 0.0044 \text{ g} \times \frac{1000 \text{ mg}}{1 \text{ g}} = 4.4 \text{ mg}
\]

Thus, there are \(\boxed{4.4 \text{ mg}}\) of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Phos-Flur Rinse.
