   - Perform PCA on the preprocessed data. This will generate a set of principal coordinates (principal variables) that represent the linear combinations of the original variables (temperature, humidity, pH, and other factors).
   - The first principal coordinate typically explains the most variation in the data, followed by the second, and so on.

