","To find the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Phos-Flur Rinse, we can use the formula:

\[
\text{Mass} = \text{Concentration} \times \text{Volume}
\]

Given:
- Concentration = 0.044% (w/v) = 0.044 g/100 mL
- Volume = 10 mL

Substitute the values into the formula:

\[
\text{Mass} = \left(\frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}}\right) \times 10 \text{ mL}
\]

\[
\text{Mass} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
\]

Convert grams to milligrams:

\[
