1. **Understand the concentration**: 0.044% (w/v) means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride per 100 mL of solution.
2. **Calculate for 10 mL**: 
   \[
   \text{Amount of sodium fluoride} = \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} \times 10 \text{ mL} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
   \]
3. **Convert grams to milligrams**:
   \[
   0.0044 \text{ g} = 4.4 \text{ mg}
   \]
