\[
\text{Mass} = \left(\frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}}\right) \times 10 \text{ mL}
\]

\[
\text{Mass} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
\]

Convert grams to milligrams:

\[
\text{Mass} = 0.0044 \text{ g} \times \frac{1000 \text{ mg}}{1 \text{ g}} = 4.4 \text{ mg}
\]

Thus, there are \(\boxed{4.4 \text{ mg}}\) of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Phos-Flur Rinse.

