The time required to reach 50°C can be found by rearranging the lumped parameter equation:  
\[
t = \frac{mc}{hA} \ln\left(\frac{T_0 - T_a}{T(t) - T_a}\right)
\]  
Substituting the values:  
\[
t = \frac{1.2 \times 385}{56.8 \times 0.075} \ln\left(\frac{345 - 20}{50 - 20}\right)
