- \(v_2 = \begin{bmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ -1 \end{bmatrix}\)
- \(v_3 = \begin{bmatrix} 0 \\ 1 \\ 1 \end{bmatrix}\)

The orthogonal matrix \([R]\) is:
\[
R = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & 0 \\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\ 1 & -1 & 1 \end{bmatrix}
\]

This is the solution for the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of \([D]\) using Jacobi's method.
