\[
q \approx \frac{1}{N!} \left( \frac{V}{\lambda^3} \right)^N e^{V/\lambda^3}
\]
For \( \lambda^3 \ll V \), the exponential term dominates, and the partition function simplifies to:
\[
q \approx \left( \frac{V}{\lambda^3} \right)^N
\]
Thus, the partition function for a high temperature ideal gas with negligible de Broglie wavelength is:
\[
\boxed{q \approx \left( \frac{V}{\lambda^3} \right)^N}
