\]
where \(V_{T0}\) is the threshold voltage at \(V_{BS} = 0\), and \(C_o\) is the oxide capacitance per unit area. The oxide capacitance is given by:
\[
C_o = \frac{1}{C_o} = \frac{1}{4 \pi \varepsilon_0 \varepsilon_o}
\]
where \(\varepsilon_0\) is the permittivity of free space and \(\varepsilon_o\) is the oxide dielectric constant. Substituting the given values:
\[
C_o = \frac{1}{4 \pi \times 8.854 \times 10^{-12} \times 0.5} = 1.78 \times 10^{-11} \text{ F/cm}^2
\]
The threshold voltage shift is:
\[
\Delta V_T = -1.0 \text{ V}
\]
The body-to-source voltage is:
\[
V_{BS} = \frac{1}{2} \left( \frac{1}{2} \right)^{1/2} \frac{N_d}{C_o} \left( \frac{1}{2} \right)^{1/2} \left( \frac{1}{2} \right)^{1/2}
\]
